' Singleton-diamond fixture — DIAMOND ARM 2 (depth 1; reaches the singleton
' at depth 2) AND the A7 blob carrier.
'
' Second independent path to sgl_shared_state, so the singleton is declared
' by three different objects in total.
'
' The DAT FILE below is the row-A7 test surface: these bytes are loaded from
' disk at compile time and written into this object's binary, but nothing
' about the blob appears in this file's source. Edit sgl_cfg_defaults.dat
' alone and a cache that keys only on source will serve a binary carrying the
' OLD blob, with no diagnostic.
'
' Note the grammar: FILE takes no BYTE/WORD/LONG keyword — the compiler forces
' byte width itself (spinResolver.ts sets wordSize before reading the name).
'
' The blob is named .dat, NOT .bin, on purpose: .gitignore:193 ignores *.bin
' project-wide because .bin is a compiler OUTPUT extension here. A blob named
' .bin would be silently left out of the repo, and every test that reads it
' would fail on a clean clone with "DAT file not found".
OBJ
  shared : "sgl_shared_state"

DAT
  cfgblob       file    "sgl_cfg_defaults.dat"

PUB start() : ok
  ok := shared.init()

PUB defaults_addr() : addr
  addr := @cfgblob

PUB reading() : value
  value := shared.count()
